      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a great use of a custom fake to add some fancy checks. I do think it will be easier to read and debug, though, if you added more asserts instead of relying on a catch-all at the end. I believe this would be logically equivalent, but provide more clarity on where things failed:\n\n```\n\tif (power_signal_set_fake.call_count \u003d\u003d 1) {\n\t    zassert_true(signal \u003d\u003d PWR_EC_PCH_RSMRST \u0026\u0026 value \u003d\u003d 0,\n\t                 \"First call but signal\u003d%d, value\u003d%d\",\n\t                 signal, value);\n\t    return 0;\n\t} else if (power_signal_set_fake.call_count \u003d\u003d 2) {\n\t    zassert_true(signal \u003d\u003d PWR_EN_PP3300_A \u0026\u0026 value \u003d\u003d 0,\n\t                 \"Second call but signal\u003d%d, value\u003d%d\",\n\t                 signal, value);\n\t    return 0;\n\t}\n\n        /* No further calls are expected */\n\tzassert_unreachable(\"Wrong input received\");\n\treturn -1;\n```",
